#: .\templates\landing.html:83
msgid "Example only. Not a real student."
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\landing.html:94
msgid "terms a year, September to June, as Somali schools run"
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\landing.html:98
msgid "grades from A to F, with boundaries each school sets itself"
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\landing.html:102
msgid "marks can be changed without a permanent record of who changed them"
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\landing.html:106
msgid "automated tests, run on every change to the software"
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\landing.html:115
msgid ""
"Replaces the paper register and the spreadsheet on one teacher's laptop."
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\landing.html:120
msgid "Marks become results on their own"
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\landing.html:122
msgid ""
"A teacher types 32 out of 40 and 51 out of 60. GradeVault works out the "
"total, the percentage, the letter grade, the term average and the position "
"in class. Nobody adds up a column by hand, so nobody makes an arithmetic "
"mistake that changes a child's standing."
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\landing.html:127
msgid "Every change is recorded"
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\landing.html:129
msgid ""
"When a mark changes, GradeVault records who changed it, when, and what it "
"was before. Nothing can edit or delete that record — not a teacher, not a "
"head teacher, not the person running the system. A school can prove a grade "
"is the one its teacher entered."
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\landing.html:134
msgid "Results appear when the school says so"
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\landing.html:136
msgid ""
"Teachers enter and correct marks freely. Students see nothing until an "
"administrator publishes the term. No child learns their result the moment a "
"teacher happens to save a page."
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\landing.html:141
msgid "Each school is separate"
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\landing.html:143
msgid ""
"Many schools can use one installation, and none of them can see another's "
"students, marks or staff. This is checked by tests that deliberately try to "
"reach another school's records and must fail."
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\landing.html:148
msgid "Report cards that print"
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\landing.html:150
msgid ""
"One student, one term, on one page: subjects, marks, grades, position, and "
"space for the class teacher, head teacher and parent to sign. It prints as a "
"document, not as a web page with menus down the side."
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\landing.html:155
msgid "Built for the connection you have"
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\landing.html:157
msgid ""
"Pages are small and plain, with no app to download and nothing that needs a "
"fast connection. A parent on a phone in Mogadishu sees the same thing as a "
"head teacher at a desk."
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\landing.html:171
msgid "The school sets itself up"
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\landing.html:173
msgid ""
"An administrator enters the year, its two terms, the classes, the subjects "
"and the school's own grading scale. Class names are whatever the school uses "
"— Class 5, Form 2, or anything else."
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\landing.html:178
msgid "Teachers record marks"
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\landing.html:180
msgid ""
"Each teacher sees only the classes and subjects they were given, and fills "
"in a mark sheet for them. A mark higher than the paper is out of is refused "
"before it can be saved."
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\landing.html:185
msgid "The school publishes the term"
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\landing.html:187
msgid ""
"When the results are ready, an administrator releases them. Students sign in "
"with their own student number and see their subjects, grades, average and "
"position, and can print a report card."
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\landing.html:196
msgid "Keeping children's records safe"
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\landing.html:198
msgid ""
"These are records about children, so the plain answers matter more than the "
"promises."
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\landing.html:202
msgid "Can a teacher see another class's marks?"
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\landing.html:203
msgid ""
"No. A teacher reaches only the subjects and classes they were assigned, and "
"this is refused whether they open the page or send the form directly."
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\landing.html:205
msgid "Can a student see a classmate's results?"
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\landing.html:206
msgid ""
"No. A student's own page carries no way to name another student, so there is "
"nothing to change in order to try."
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\landing.html:208
msgid "Can a grade be changed quietly?"
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\landing.html:209
msgid ""
"No. Every change writes a record that nothing in the system is able to edit "
"or remove."
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\landing.html:211
msgid "Are passwords readable by staff?"
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\landing.html:212
msgid ""
"No. Passwords are stored scrambled in a way that cannot be reversed. An "
"administrator can set a new one; nobody can read the old one."
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\landing.html:214
msgid "Can someone guess a student's password?"
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\landing.html:215
msgid ""
"Repeated wrong attempts pause sign-in for that account and device. One "
"student being locked out never locks out their classmates, even on a shared "
"school connection."
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\landing.html:219
msgid ""
"One thing said plainly: GradeVault has not yet been examined by security "
"specialists from outside the project. Before any school entrusts it with "
"real records, it should be."
msgstr ""

#: .\templates\landing.html:226
msgid "Ready to look inside?"
msgstr ""

